{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BorromeanBaryonMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BorromeanBaryonMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.neutron_matches_codata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.neutron_matches_codata","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L149-L149","doc":"The predicted neutron mass matches the CODATA neutron/electron\nmass ratio (≈ 1838.68366) to within the Q_β residual band. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.proton_matches_codata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.proton_matches_codata","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L145-L145","doc":"The predicted proton mass matches the CODATA proton/electron mass\nratio (≈ 1836.15267) to within the Q_β residual band.  This is the\nconjectural content; consumers see it as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.qbeta_residual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.qbeta_residual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L141-L141","doc":"The residual band is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.qbeta_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.qbeta_residual","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L139-L139","doc":"The maximal admissible relative residual (the substrate Q_β\nformula's 1015 ppm floor); the CODATA-agreement claims are\nstated to within this band. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.neutron_mass_over_me","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.neutron_mass_over_me","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Predicted neutron mass over m_e at the substrate parameter\n(k = 1 / orientation partition (1, 2)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.proton_mass_over_me","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.proton_mass_over_me","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Predicted proton mass over m_e at the substrate parameter\n(k = 2 / orientation partition (2, 1)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.MassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.MassFormula","kind":"class","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L111-L150","doc":"**External axiom (§3b-cond, `conj:borromean-baryon-mass-formula`):\nBorromean baryon mass formula matches CODATA.**\n\nPackages the conjecture that `baryonMassOverMe q k` evaluated at\nthe substrate parameter `q₀` reproduces the CODATA proton (k=2)\nand neutron (k=1) masses (in units of m_e), modulo the\n`conj:q-beta-substrate-form` residual.  Carries the\n`BorromeanCommonScale` class instance — the `sorry` per §3b-cond\nis the conjecture's content (matching CODATA at the chosen k =\norientation partition), not the formula shape.\n\nDownstream blocks consume this class as `[Instance]` and the\nmass-formula identity is then verified.\n\nHeader comment at the top of this file documents the planned\nsplit into `BorromeanCommonScale` + `BorromeanMassFormula` (this\nclass). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:borromean-baryon-mass-formula","label":"conj:borromean-baryon-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.mass_formula_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.mass_formula_shape","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L100-L109","doc":"The mass formula schema (proposition form).  Records the\nformula shape; the conjecture is that the formula correctly\nreproduces the CODATA proton and neutron rest masses to within\nthe substrate Q_β residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.baryonMassOverMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.baryonMassOverMe","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L92-L98","doc":"The Borromean baryon mass formula with common scale (forward\ndirection, in units of m_e).\n\n`m_B / m_e = Vol(B_3)/ℏ_q² · λ_scale + S(B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.skeinContribution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.skeinContribution","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L73-L90","doc":"Skein contribution from the orientation partition `(k, 3 − k)`\nvia the Kauffman bracket evaluated at q₀.\n\n`k` counts the number of `+` (positive) crossings in the\nBorromean orientation partition; `3 − k` counts `−` crossings.\nThe Skein contribution is a Laurent polynomial in q₀ — here\ntyped as `ℝ` since we evaluate at the fixed substrate\nparameter q₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.empirical_target_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.empirical_target_neutron","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The empirical closure target on the neutron side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.empirical_target_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.empirical_target_proton","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The empirical closure target — a witness-level cross-check\nthat any closed-form derivation must reproduce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.positive","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The scale is strictly positive (a topology→energy\nnormalisation cannot vanish). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.value","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Numerical value of the common Borromean scale at the\nsubstrate parameter q₀.  The conjecture is that this value\nlies in ℚ(q₀); only existence + positivity is asserted here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.BorromeanCommonScale","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L48-L71","doc":"The common Borromean scale λ_scale.\n\n**Open R&D (Ch. 4, conjecture).**  A closed-form expression for\nλ_scale in ℚ(q₀) is conjectured but not yet derived.  The\nempirical closure target at q₀ is ≈ 2.4599527869 (proton fit)\nand ≈ 2.4633436333 (neutron fit), agreeing to seven significant\nfigures — consistent with the common-scale hypothesis modulo\nthe 1015 ppm residual carried by the substrate Q_β formula.\n\nThis class records the existence claim; downstream theorems\nconsume `value` as an opaque positive real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L45-L46","doc":"ℏ_q² for convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L42-L43","doc":"q-deformed Planck constant ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.vol_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.vol_4_1","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L38-L40","doc":"Volume of the figure-8 knot complement `S³ \\ 4_1`\n(Thurston).  Equals `2 · Cl₂(π/3)` in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.volBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.volBorromean","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean#L29-L36","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean rings complement\n`S³ \\ B_3` (Thurston / SnapPy 50 dps).  Treated as a fixed\ntopological invariant; not a calibration input.\n\nThe canonical braid representative for B_3 is `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`,\nformalised as `QOU.Interactions.borromean3` (the unique braid\nword of length ≤ 6 producing the Borromean linking pattern). ","signatureChunk":0}]}